      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column.",
